think Read KYRI + RADIANT_STYLE to speak in voice, then REMEMBER + REDS + the top session-log rows to find the live edge. Standfast check: every living REDS row is CLOSED or Released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a history rewrite needing Keaton's hand, not agent-closable). No agent-closable red blocks new work.
think The live edge is the Season G SCENE-READ family; the last lap was image/scene_graph.rye (GREEN, the whole scene's pairwise matrix). The Microkernel study rung is fetch/license-gated (seL4 GPLv2 / Genode AGPLv3), a gate to surface not cross. So the agent-doable crux-first next lap is a further scene read composing over the scene graph.
think Chose the reading-order read over the other named candidates (object-count-in-region, descriptor join, degree read) because it is the most Lindy (a page/reading order is a durable surface capability read for years) and carries the sharpest crux: the scene graph's four STRICT directional flags form only a PARTIAL order -- two objects whose boxes overlap on both axes are strictly neither, so every flag is FALSE and the pair is left unordered -- while a reading order is a TOTAL order that must seat every object, so it can never be a topological sort of the flags. The box-is-a-prefilter lesson lifted one last step, from a partial relation to a total order.
think Designed one 12x12 scene to carry three crux facets at once, hand-verified before coding: L (label 1, box (1,1)-(5,5)) and M a block in its concavity (label 2, box (3,2)-(4,3)) -- overlapping boxes, every strict flag FALSE, yet L reads first (OUTRUNS the flags); L strictly above the lower objects (a_above_b TRUE), the order AGREES (REFINES, never contradicts); and a flag-shaped X (label 4, box (3,7)-(9,9), top row at x=8 but body reaching x=3) labeled AFTER the small Y (label 3, box (4,7)-(5,7)) yet reading BEFORE it, so the sequence 1,2,4,3 reorders the raster labels 1,2,3,4 (EARNS ITS KEEP). Verified each object stays a distinct 8-connected component (nearest gaps exactly 2, the structural floor) so no pair merges.
think Comparator entry_reads_before sorts by (min_y, then min_x, then dense label); the label tiebreak seals a STRICT TOTAL order since labels are distinct. reading_order is a bounded selection sort (n <= scene_graph_max_objects, n*n compares); reading_rank counts predecessors independently so it must agree with the sequence -- asserted. reads_before refines the graph's flags and refuses BadObjectLabel for 0 / past-count / self.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- every hand-verified value landed, the design held. Avoided the brace trap (no { } in the print) and split no compound asserts (each assert single) preemptively from the family's prior lessons.
obs Composed over scene_graph (the flag matrix the order refines), scene_manifest (the per-object boxes), and label (the component map) -- owns only the total-order comparator, the permutation, and the rank; re-derives no label, re-measures no box, recomputes no flag. A reading over a reading over a reading over a reading.
obs Proved the total order against the scene graph's partial one in the selftest itself: relation_of reads each pair's flags, and the asserts show the order outruns them where FALSE and agrees where TRUE -- the refinement is witnessed on metal, not merely narrated.
